    "result_text": "All tests pass. The change is complete. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nOwner deletion is now a **soft-delete**. `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` flags the owner `deleted` and retains the row; `GET` still returns it (with `deleted: true`); and the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks ignore deleted owners.\n\n### Changes\n\n**Domain / schema**\n- `model/Owner.java` \u2014 added a `boolean deleted` field (mapped to a `deleted` column) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`. A new owner defaults to `false`.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added a `deleted` column with `DEFAULT FALSE`/`DEFAULT 0` NOT NULL, so seed rows come back `false`. (Tests run on hsqldb; I updated all four for consistency.)\n- `resources/openapi.yml` \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\n**Behavior**\n- `rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`\n  - `deleteOwner`: now sets `deleted = true` and saves (returns `204`, a 2xx) instead of removing the record.\n  - `isDuplicateOwner` and `possibleDuplicateOf`: skip owners flagged `deleted`.\n- `rest/controller/HouseholdResolver.java` \u2014 `householdExists` skips deleted owners (this is the household-duplicate check that would otherwise block re-creating a soft-deleted owner).\n\n### Tests\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 both `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` (the full suite) pass.\n\nI scoped the `deleted` filter to the duplicate/identity checks only, per the spec (\"duplicate and identity checks must then ignore owners flagged deleted\"), leaving the count-based quota rules (per-day, per-city, namesake, customer-code dedup) untouched.",
